  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Possible condition",
     "texto": [
      "For a real or open possibility, use **si + présent** and then the **futur**: **Si j'ai le temps, je voyagerai** (if I have time, I will travel)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Hypothesis",
     "texto": [
      "For an imagined or unlikely situation, use **si + imparfait** and then the **conditionnel**: **Si j'avais le temps, je voyagerais** (if I had time, I would travel).",
      "The order can change: **Je voyagerais si j'avais le temps.**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Note",
     "texto": [
      "In these two conditional structures, the verb in the part with **si** is not in the futur or the conditionnel.",
      "The rule does not apply to all uses of **si**: in an indirect question any necessary tense can appear, including the conditionnel: **Je me demande si tu pourrais venir**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Condition (si + imparfait)",
     "columnas": [
